problem:
Problem description
- There are $$P$$ products indexed by $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$ and $$R$$ production processes indexed by $$r \in \mathcal{R}$$.
- The planning horizon is one weekly period, represented by $$\mathcal{T}$$, and the model determines a weekly production plan.
- Each product uses process time according to a processing-time matrix $$a_{r,p}$$; a zero entry means that product does not use that process.
- Each process has an available weekly capacity $$C_r$$ and an hourly operating cost $$c_r$$.
- Each product has a selling price per unit $$s_p$$.
- The weekly profit is the total sales revenue from produced units minus the operating cost of all used process hours.
- A minimum output requirement may be imposed for selected products through a lower-bound vector $$\ell_p$$; in this problem, at least one product has a positive lower bound.
- A minimum profit target $$\Pi^{\min}$$ must be met by the weekly plan.
- Overtime is not allowed, so no process may use more than its available weekly capacity.
- Idle time means unused capacity on each process, and lower idle time is preferred with weights proportional to the corresponding hourly costs $$c_r$$.
- The optimization goal is to choose weekly production quantities that maximize weekly profit while satisfying all capacity, production, and profit requirements, and while keeping weighted idle time as low as possible among feasible plans.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_p$$: weekly production quantity of product $$p$$.
  - $$u_r$$: idle time of process $$r$$ during the week.
  - $$\Pi$$: achieved total weekly profit.
  - $$\mathbf{x} = \{x_p\}_{p \in \mathcal{P}}$$ together with $$\mathbf{u} = \{u_r\}_{r \in \mathcal{R}}$$ as the complete production plan.

Input Format
{
  "num_products": "$$P$$",
  "num_processes": "$$R$$",
  "products": {
    "index_set": "$$\\mathcal{P} = \\{1,2,\\ldots,P\\}$$",
    "meaning": "Set of products."
  },
  "processes": {
    "index_set": "$$\\mathcal{R} = \\{1,2,\\ldots,R\\}$$",
    "meaning": "Set of production processes."
  },
  "planning_horizon": {
    "periods": "$$\\mathcal{T}$$",
    "meaning": "Weekly planning period; the base problem uses a single week."
  },
  "processing_time": {
    "shape": "$$R \\times P$$",
    "symbol": "$$a_{r,p}$$",
    "meaning": "Hours required from process $$r$$ to produce one unit of product $$p$$."
  },
  "capacity": {
    "shape": "$$R$$",
    "symbol": "$$C_r$$",
    "meaning": "Available weekly capacity in hours for each process $$r$$."
  },
  "hourly_cost": {
    "shape": "$$R$$",
    "symbol": "$$c_r$$",
    "meaning": "Hourly operating cost of each process $$r$$."
  },
  "selling_price": {
    "shape": "$$P$$",
    "symbol": "$$s_p$$",
    "meaning": "Unit selling price of each product $$p$$."
  },
  "minimum_profit": {
    "symbol": "$$\\Pi^{\\min}$$",
    "meaning": "Minimum required weekly profit."
  },
  "minimum_production": {
    "shape": "$$P$$",
    "symbol": "$$\\ell_p$$",
    "meaning": "Minimum weekly production requirement for each product $$p$$; entries may be zero when no lower bound is required."
  },
  "idle_time_weight": {
    "shape": "$$R$$",
    "symbol": "$$w_r$$",
    "meaning": "Weight used for idle-time minimization on each process $$r$$, typically proportional to $$c_r$$."
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "production_plan": {
    "shape": "$$P$$",
    "symbol": "$$x_p$$",
    "meaning": "Weekly production quantity of each product $$p$$."
  },
  "idle_time": {
    "shape": "$$R$$",
    "symbol": "$$u_r$$",
    "meaning": "Unused weekly capacity time for each process $$r$$."
  },
  "total_profit": {
    "symbol": "$$\\Pi$$",
    "meaning": "Achieved total weekly profit of the selected plan."
  },
  "feasibility_status": {
    "meaning": "Indicates whether the returned plan satisfies all production, capacity, and profit requirements."
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "num_products": 2,
  "num_processes": 3,
  "products": ["Type A", "Type B"],
  "processes": ["Manufacturing", "Assembly", "Inspection"],
  "planning_horizon": "1 week",
  "processing_time": [
    [20, 0],
    [5, 7],
    [3, 6]
  ],
  "capacity": [120, 80, 40],
  "hourly_cost": [12, 8, 10],
  "selling_price": [650, 725],
  "minimum_profit": 3000,
  "minimum_production": [5, 0],
  "idle_time_weight": [12, 8, 10]
}
